# 🌑 AETHERIA — GAME STATE SYSTEM

> **The Game State System is the memory, condition, and evolution layer of Aetheria.**
>
> Every action changes the state of the world.
>
> Every state can create consequences.
>
> Every consequence can change the future.

---

# 📌 1. OVERVIEW

The **Game State System** is one of the most important core systems in Aetheria.

It is responsible for managing the current condition of:

```text
core World building
Master
Characters
Enemies
Items
Inventory
Factions
Locations
Tower
Floors
Quests
Events
Relationships
Resources
Story
Destruction floor
Time-dependent states
```

The Game State System does not exist to replace other systems.

Instead, it acts as the central state-management layer that connects them.

```text
                         GAME MANAGER
                              │
                              ▼
                     GAME STATE SYSTEM
                              │
       ┌──────────────────────┼──────────────────────┐
       │                      │                      │
       ▼                      ▼                      ▼
  WORLD STATE            ENTITY STATE           SYSTEM STATE
       │                      │                      │
       ├── World              ├── Master            ├── Quest
       ├── Tower              ├── Character         ├── Event
       ├── Floor              ├── Enemy             ├── Recruit
       ├── Faction            ├── Item              ├── Dungeon
       └── Destruction                              └── Inventory
                              │
                              ▼
                       DATABASE SYSTEM
```

---

# 🎯 2. PRIMARY PURPOSE

The Game State System answers the most important question:

> **"What is happening in Aetheria right now?"**

For example:

```text
Master:
Floor 20
Level 20
HP 850
Gold 12,500

Character:
CHAR_000125
Level 25
HP 100%

Enemy:
ENEMY_000451
Status: Defeated

Faction:
Cult Influence: 62%

World:
Destruction: 71%

Time:
Day 35 — 21:45
```

All of these are part of the current Game State.

The Master does not use EXP.

The Master Level increases by spending Gold through the Master Level Upgrade System.

---

# 🧠 3. CORE PRINCIPLE

The Game State System follows:

> **Every meaningful change in the game must produce a state change.**

Example:

```text
Enemy defeated
       ↓
Enemy State
       ↓
Loot generated
       ↓
Inventory State
       ↓
Quest State
       ↓
World State
       ↓
Database
```

A single action can therefore affect multiple states.

The Master does not gain EXP from combat, quests, training, or other activities.

The Master Level increases only through a Gold-based upgrade.

```text
Gold Spent
       ↓
Master Level Upgrade Validation
       ↓
Gold Deducted
       ↓
Master Level Increased
       ↓
Database
```

